    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0308" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v06p1/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.5/1–1353</note>
                <head>No. 146<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Director for Mutual Security
                            (Tannenwald)
                        to the Under Secretary of State (Bruce)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-01-13">January 13, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear David</hi>: You will recall that about a week ago you and I
                    discussed again the question of a circular airgram on the subject of European
                        integration.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d146-f1"/> I indicated to you at that time
                    that we had reservations about the failure of the State Department draft to set
                    forth clearly the need for United States support and encouragement of progress
                    toward integration.</p>
                <p>You suggested that we prepare a redraft of the cable which would incorporate our
                    views. I have had this redraft prepared and am enclosing a copy herewith,
                    together with a copy of a memorandum to me from Harlan Cleveland, dated January 10,
                    1953, which deals with the redraft.</p>
                <p>In view of the present crisis in European integration and the fact that the new
                    Administration will take office in a week, I seriously question the advisability
                    of sending such a cable at the present time. However, I believe that the problem
                    of European integration is one that should promptly be dealt with by the new
                    Administration and perhaps the enclosed draft cable will facilitate the reaching
                    of a decision.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Ted</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d146-a1.xml" xpointer="d146-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d146-a2.xml" xpointer="d146-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
